{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages","id":929782,"title":"Tasks for Novice mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-11T09:14:02-07:00","id":929782,"title":"Tasks for Novice mages","content":"I running game of freshly Awakened mages in Boston. As I want to play a bit with Order training of characters and coming after \u2018Show, Don\u2019t Tell\u2019 advice on introducing setting NPCs \u2013 I thought that sending young PCs on \u2018errands\u2019 to various cabals of city would be great way to do this. <b>But I have problem with low power demanding tasks for fresh mages \u2013 could you help me with them?</b><br /> <br /> PCs are under protection of <i>Khumeia</i>, Boston Councilor and Silver Ladder Deacon \u2013 and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=826830#post826830\">her cabal <i>Illuminated Pentad</i></a>. What could Magister like her or her cabal mates need characters to do for them based on interactions with other cabals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T09:41:32-07:00","id":929791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages#post929782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I running game of freshly Awakened mages in Boston. As I want to play a bit with Order training of characters and coming after \u2018Show, Don\u2019t Tell\u2019 advice on introducing setting NPCs \u2013 I thought that sending young PCs on \u2018errands\u2019 to various cabals of city would be great way to do this. <b>But I have problem with low power demanding tasks for fresh mages \u2013 could you help me with them?</b><br /> <br /> PCs are under protection of <i>Khumeia</i>, Boston Councilor and Silver Ladder Deacon \u2013 and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=826830#post826830\">her cabal <i>Illuminated Pentad</i></a>. What could Magister like her or her cabal mates need characters to do for them based on interactions with other cabals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I LIVE IN BOSTON!<br /> <br /> Sorry, just moved here literally a week ago. ANYWHO.<br /> <br /> For new mages, especially Silver Ladder, I typically have PCs have to run errands like deliver or retrieving things, filling out paperwork, etc, on behalf of their mentor or whoever's responsible for them. Something could go wrong in the midst of that, if you want conflict, or you could have most things go well and just keep it a training type thing. I like to show the tediousness and bureaucracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T09:46:50-07:00","id":929793,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you don't have to make it challenging to make it a good introduction. It makes sense that newbies usually don't get sent on difficult tasks until they've proven they can handle them. Most challenges probably arise from the newbies themselves treading into waters deeper and darker than they anticipated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:18:49-07:00","id":929804,"title":"","content":"I get that they should be easy tasks on behalf of mentor - <b>But can someone put <i>examples</i> of those needed in Awakened community?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:24:28-07:00","id":929807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=929804#post929804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that they should be easy tasks on behalf of mentor - <b>But can someone put <i>examples</i> of those needed in Awakened community?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Filing paperwork. Delivering Council decrees or judgments for mages who have stepped out of line (accompanied by Sentinels or other more experienced mages). Answering phone calls. Handling Sleepwalker retainers. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 07-11-2016, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:57:45-07:00","id":929833,"title":"","content":"I would have novice mages investigate things. The paperwork, message running and other council business is just a front to get the players into the real story. Put something interesting or dangerous in their path and see how they deal with it. You can get a lot of mileage out of various one dot investigation spells when you have two dots in an arcana, and mage sight is all about investigating mysteries. Alternatively a PC could run into a mundane crime, getting caught up in that but find that something supernatural caused it. A spirit possessing someone to steal something for example. Combat should be against groups of street thugs or one or two higher point types. Investigations should be against the minions of enemies that will show up later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:09:37-07:00","id":929841,"title":"","content":"A retainer in service to Khumeia dies and she asks them to find out what happened. It could be caused by something totally mundane, but players will have fun figuring out how to find out, get the info, and then deliver it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:23:33-07:00","id":929891,"title":"","content":"Instead of &quot;dies&quot;, I would go with &quot;isn't answering phone calls, that lazy bastard&quot;, which could lead into something bigger (especially if you can isolate them from means of getting help, like by transporting them into a twisted dimension or something). <br /> It would be good first to create expectations of nothing-weird happening by making it looking like another quest in a chain of filler quests before &quot;something happens&quot; - a good technique for this is to create expectations, for example<br /> &quot;Finish 4 tasks for me, and I will take you on a real mission&quot; - players are going to either expect that 1st, 2nd, or 4th mission will have complications, because they will think that real deal will start after end of the tutorial. So you subvert it by doing it at 3rd task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:02:15-07:00","id":929918,"title":"","content":"I <i>do not</i> want to make game in to '<b>Errand Boy: The Assistant</b>' - still want game to feel as <b>Mage</b> - I wanted to highlight one or two tasks made into game stories ( 'On one of those things you do for her, from last two weeks...' ).<br /> <br /> Not to mention that even Silver Ladder would not made mages do things that Sleepers could easily done from Cryptopoly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silver Ladder, p.102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Promising young willworkers have been watched carefully and tested thoroughly, and the mentor or foster cabal almost always provides an extensive portfolio of the potential member\u2019s achievements. If the novice meets the approval of the caucus, the mentor or foster cabal returns to her with an offer of membership, coupled with a task of initiation. The task is rarely terribly difficult, is usually of a social or political nature (though often a mixture of the two), and provides the initiate an opportunity to put her understanding of the Lesser Elemental Precepts into action. As the recruit fulfills the task of initiation, her mentor guides her to a basic understanding of the Greater Elemental Precepts.<br /> <br /> Initiation tasks are usually goal-oriented. A typical task may be securing a specific position in a specific company. The task may be given in a straightforward manner (\u201cWe need you to become the head of IT at Enrond Electronics\u201d), though it is more often laid out in a more circuitous manner (\u201cWe need you to gain long-term influence over the way internal systems are analyzed and repaired at Enrond Elec-tronics\u201d). A recruit who finds a creative method of completing the task is often granted a great deal of respect, relative to her experience, from the moment she undergoes the induction rite (see below). Use of magic during the task, however, is strongly frowned upon, and an obvious reliance upon magic to complete the task is grounds for reconsideration of membership. Th\u00e9archs are expected to be able to stand on their own two feet when the use of magic isn\u2019t an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:20:39-07:00","id":929932,"title":"","content":"The Illuminated Pentad's interests are a good starting point. Khumeia has her bankers, socialites and the IRS, Thanatos has his ghosts and Faustina has her construction companies. Since they have run their operations for quite some time the PCs aren't needed for the daily upkeep. However, if anything unusual crops up, they can be sent to investigate:<br /> <br /> - Khumeia's IRS ally has been suffering from missing time and their work performance has gone down as a result.<br /> - Thanatos's Ghosts are reporting poltergeist-like activity but can't pinpoint anyone responsible.<br /> - One of Faustina's geomantic projects is experiencing delays and Fate magic has been detected.<br /> <br /> Then, make one of the other Cabals responsible. This needn't be malicious. When confronted they have a good explanation, or give an apology and fix the problem. The man from the IRS saw something they shouldn't and had their memory edited. A Spirit controlled by someone else got trapped by their Ban/Bane and is acting out. As an unintended consequence, a Blessing cast on a Sleeper had them benefit from the construction delays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:44:15-07:00","id":929945,"title":"","content":"In my chronicle the first task their mentor gave them was a cryptid hunt, currently too minor a problem to attract higher interest but a good thing to nip in the bud before it became a problem. In Soul Cages DaveB had his players track down a problematic ghost sighting.<br /> Boston Unveiled mentioned rats being stirred up by the big dig, have a group of rats do something odd, then assign your players to investigate with orders to determine if it was just wild chance or if there might be something bigger beneath the surface. Such an investigation would send them scurrying through the territories of multiple cabals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:55:24-07:00","id":929950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=929945#post929945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such an investigation would send them scurrying through the territories of multiple cabals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Upvoted for killing all the birds with one stone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:00:55-07:00","id":930186,"title":"","content":"Chronicles main Mystery is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/668690-mystery-supernal-alchemy-philosopher-s-stone?p=876709#post876709\">Philosopher Stones</a> PCs got from Nicolas Flamel as 'Sleepers'. They also get his Uncrowned Kings Daimonomicons. As <i>Khumeia</i> and her cabal is dedicated to Alchemy, I was thinking maybe basing tasks on this. Something like taking Grimoire in exotic language ( like High Speech ) to the <i>Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth</i> for translation as main Mysterium cabal, or something. But then I remember that <i>Khumeia</i> is Adept of Mind and she would not need any service like this, when she just can cast simple spell... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-12-2016, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:14:38-07:00","id":930193,"title":"","content":"How populous is your Mage setting? Are there many Mages running around, both novice and experienced, or are they relatively rare, especially compared to Sleepwalker and brainwashed cultist retainers? It's important to take a stance on this, because novices and newbies will be given different tasks if there are, like, 1000 of them running around, and if newcomer Mages are relatively rare and you get maybe 1-2 every few years, they will be given much more care and probably won't be wasted on paper pushing stuff.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that for novices, I would steer away from plots and tasks involving other Mages. Mage is pretty complicated, and interacting with other Mages is even more complicated; a good initial playground is one where Mages interact with non-Mages and problems that aren't necessarily generated by other Mages.<br /> Mostly because, as you noted, other Mages can and probably will just solve the issue with a spell.<br /> <br /> Checking up on ongoing projects that are being overwatched by Sleepwalker retainers is a good starting point; it doesn't involve other Mages directly (so they can't solve problems for PCs), and still explores and involves the Mage society.<br /> And of course, there are probably some Mysteries that mentors of your PCs don't have time to take care of, because TIME IS MONEY and they are too busy with something closer to their personal Obsession....but they still called dibs on in order to use them as tokens of political power later. Or as food for newbies.<br /> <br /> Actually, you might send them to investigate some minor Mystery that was &quot;left for later&quot; and figure out that someone is actually trying to solve it under the radar, thinking that no one will notice. Then they can see what kind of traces a sloppy mage lefts behind and track it back to the offender. It's a relatively fun way to explore Magic Sight, Unveiling and Knowing Spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:27:03-07:00","id":930200,"title":"","content":"maybe she wants a translated copy so that she doesn't have to cast a spell every time she wants to check something.<br /> Or<br /> She sends them get a grimoire she has recently negotiated a price for (they would be carrying whatever she has promised in exchange with them to make the trade).<br /> Or<br /> She sends them with a letter of request to another Mage/Cabal. Someone who would think it impolite to be approached by phone or e-mail, or someone who needs a little incentive to agree to the request (so the PCs will be carrying a bri... Incentive)<br /> <br /> In the case of them carrying something valuable either way, complications can arise from that, especially if it's alive (which could turn into the cryptic hunt suggested above) or if it has very particular rules as to how it should be handled.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also remember that Mages aren't above giving tasks that seem to be about one thing but that is really about something else. A task stated to be about collecting signatures or securing votes in the consilium could really be about having the PCs become accquainted with the different cabals in the area (perhaps with the idea of questioning them afterwards to see what their impressions are/what those cabals seem to be up to).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/983-mirrorscape","name":"Mirrorscape","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:44:09-07:00","id":930208,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/983-mirrorscape\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar983_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"983\" data-vbnamecard=\"983\">Mirrorscape</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6084\" data-vbnamecard=\"6084\">2ptTakrill</a> - Thanks for advice!<br /> <br /> I also need to probably point it - all PCs will end in <b><i>other</i></b> Orders than Silver Ladder of <i>Khumeia</i>. She just picked them first, as they dwelled in to her cabal Alchemy Obsession. So this mean I <i>need</i> PCs to meet other Orders mages, so they become their proper Mentors. Lucky, Silver Ladder ( like Guardians ) have tradition to give fresh mages after initial trening to other Orders if they do not jive with tearch's Elemental Precepts.<br /> <br /> So some missions with meeting Awakened are much more preferred for this particular chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-12-2016, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:48:36-07:00","id":930210,"title":"","content":"What Arcana are your players flourishing? Also, for &quot;not involving other Awakened&quot; - I meant that the problem and solving it shouldn't revolve around other Mages and Supernal problems; meeting other Mage as a background to the actual problem is a good thing. <br /> Maybe some minor wizard is paying Khumeia for protection and PC's are sent to solve some problem that minor wizard (either a very weak Awakened, or some sort of Hedge Mage) is not able to solve on their own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T07:24:34-07:00","id":930319,"title":"","content":"I think errand running is still the best way to treat this, with a starting focus on feeling at least initially mundane. If you want Mages to meet up with mentors in other Orders, have them show off their passions and beliefs in some way and let the Magister decide where they belong by introducing them to other people to do work for.<br /> <br /> Have the Thyrsus heal people, the Mastigos keep an eye on someone, etc.<br /> <br /> Then, one day, something comes up and they all have to work together. The Thyrsus encounters an outbreak of a magical disease; the Mastigos's target is murdered while clutching a tattered scroll scrawled in Aramaic. Something goes on that unites them all and makes them ask fundamental questions. Ask players what Orders they want to join, give them chances to abide that Order's philosophy. The would-be mystagogue fights to preserve the knowledge, the guardian hides the evidence of magic, the thearch speaks passionately about the need to protect and guide mortals, the fledgling revels in the challenge, the libertine... Uh... Does whatever libertines do?<br /> <br /> When it comes time to give their status report, you now have reasons for them to be introduced to new mentors; someone who needs a research assistant; the &quot;cleaner&quot; who mops up after the local cults needs a spare set of hands; a thearch running a soup kitchen could do with someone who can help with rehab; a dojo leader looks for new students; a libertine looks for another libertine to do libertine things that are libertine-ish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T15:52:03-07:00","id":931659,"title":"","content":"Whenever I send my players on an errand it invariably blows up when they least expect it and it becomes an adventure. Furthermore, I never send them on errands unless they have first gotten a favor from someone, try to get on the good side of someone they need, or if they have broken the Lex Magica. So, they still manage to get tagged for a bunch of errands of course. In general, in my style of STing I tend to make every little task interesting or dangerous: otherwise they would have sent a sleepwalker to do it. Mages need to do &quot;Mage-sized&quot; errands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T16:30:12-07:00","id":931679,"title":"","content":"There is actually one job that elder mage can perfectly do, but quickly be unwilling to due to actual costs that aren't devastating to the younglings:<br /> Managing and restarting magical infrastructure around.<br /> <br /> Basically, a lot of Mages will act like small God-Machines; trying to carry out large scale occult projects that involve a lot of legwork and lots of spells being put in motion. Spells that need to be either maintained or relinquished. Relinquishing spells permanently drops permanent willpower, so for big projects requiring a lot of individual spells this is a no no; unsafe relinquishing demands temporary Willpower, and even elder mages have only X of it at any given time.<br /> So, basically, you could have your players go and check on some magical infrastructure, make sure that these spells didn't get corrupted, deal with any potential corruption, and recast spells if possible.<br /> This way you have legwork that actually demands a mage, isn't too hard for a newbie, has a reason for elder mage to not just magically solve it, and might foreshadow something bigger for the future, or lead straight into an adventure. <br /> This obviously assumes that your Consilium doesn't consider unsafe resolving of spell a DANGEROUS CRIME!, which looked pretty weird to me anyway and little overreacting looking at the actual implementation of these rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T21:01:26-07:00","id":931793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=931679#post931679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, a lot of Mages will act like small God-Machines; trying to carry out large scale occult projects that involve a lot of legwork and lots of spells being put in motion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The concise way to say this is that Obsession is going to drive some mages to orchestrate Mysteries, and the demands of these processes is going to result in similar behavior to many Highly Mysterious entities like, say, any given Rank 6+ ephemeral being on a good day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This obviously assumes that your Consilium doesn't consider unsafe resolving of spell a DANGEROUS CRIME!, which looked pretty weird to me anyway and little overreacting looking at the actual implementation of these rules. </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's illegal, or at least considered dangerously negligent&quot; is a far cry from dangerous-crime-all-caps-exclamation-point. That's about the same view most knowledgeable societies have of toxic waste dumping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T23:30:48-07:00","id":931849,"title":"","content":"Run yesterday first session of proper mentoring by <i>Khumeia</i>. Beside talk about Atlantis, mentioning Paths, Mage Sight and general forecasting other Orders as 'Atlantean Castes', one of player showed her his Philosophers Stone and her eyes gleamed in Gollum-like way. She said she will of course help in recreating it ( whole <i>Illuminated Pentad</i> has Obsession on Philosophers Stone even before games takes place ) and she asked if they have more things from <i>Nick</i> <i>Fleming</i>, as he is great patron and teacher of Supernal Alchemy and their Legacy of <i>Uncrowned Kings</i>. Player admitted that they have books from him, but they are in the possession of character that left trening when she heard that <i>Faustina </i>hacked their Fate to meet in Boston. <i>Khumeia</i> said that as books are crucial to understand Philosophers Stone and she can arrange meeting with other mages on translating them - they need to convince other PC to give them to it. Or she will not continue to teach them.<br /> <br /> Basically, <b><i>Khumeia</i> said 'return with books or no Awakened contacts and second lesson' ( i.e. Mage Armor and Shadow Names ).</b> I have overstepped here with <i>Khumeia</i>'s stand as mentor?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2535_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2535\" data-vbnamecard=\"2535\">arthexis</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> - Good ideas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T23:48:29-07:00","id":931857,"title":"","content":"Not if the characters don't know better, though you may have it come back to haunt their relationship with her later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T02:05:14-07:00","id":931891,"title":"","content":"Less mentor more extortionist, but it's not necessarily crossing a line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T23:59:50-07:00","id":958624,"title":"","content":"So I'm in a bit dead end. After three sessions, no one of players wanted to continue mentoring in <i>Khumeia</i> - only one of character bring her ENGLISH version of Grimoires that she <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=953232#post953232\">copied by use of Matter and Prime</a> - but even this was more like demanding from her on one PC that was least stubborn and making jokes about her. So she need to send PCs to other teachers as clearly Silver Ladder is not working for them - one will go to <i>Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth</i> to join Mysterium, two will go to <i>Dead Wrens</i> to join Free Council and one is under care of <i>Shadow Chorus</i> to join Guardians of Veil.<br /> <br /> The problem I have is in connecting them once again after this split into proto-cabal. Now <i>Khumeia</i> is not their official supervisor, new mentor cabals have very different opinions about each other and Flamel's Grimoire is not driving plot for now, as only used version of Daimonomicon is in Old English, so anyone can read it ( and no need for translation then ). Before whole players mess I was planning to give them mission/favor from <i>Faustina </i>that she discovered them in first place and they are under her cabal care ( <i>Illuminated Pentad </i>), even if she is not very much on speaking terms with <i>Khumeia</i>. But now, the most I could see is <i>Faustina</i> geting to one PC and asking her for help. Task was to go to check new construction site at MIT she is making plans for as there probably is Mystery there, but also <i>Faustina</i> cannot dwell in there after dark to not lose her contract with Sleepers company.<br /> <br /> It's a best I come for now but this task has many holes and I'm afraid that players will just not pursue this idea - as they shown their stubbornness to this day. I plan in few sessions to add Promethean PC, as chronicle is about Alchemy and (s)he will be instant Obsession, but it's nothing sure for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T01:01:00-07:00","id":958633,"title":"","content":"You could have Khumeia propose that the consilium make the new magi their own cabal as a sort of training group. If you've read Broken Diamond, basically the Cruicible from that.<br /> <br /> Nominally, she can claim it's to bring cabals together to improve relations between them (and if that works, great. Khumeia gets to look good). However, more likely, the various mentors will pull the cabal apart or alternatively keep it at armslength because they don't trust the other mentors. That basically sets them up to being marginalised. As a SL Deacon I'm guessing Khumeia probably can't want to get rid of them, but I could see her being quite annoyed none the less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T01:08:17-07:00","id":958635,"title":"","content":"Question - Thing that was not clear to me in reading of <b>Sanctum &amp; Sigil</b> - <b>Do mentors need direct Consilium meeting on forming cabal?</b> Or do they only need to agree with themselves? Like, do I need to announce whole Ruling Council meeting - or just that <i>Brotherhood</i>, <i>Chorus</i> and <i>Wrens</i> meet and agree to forming the cabal from their new apprentices?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=958633#post958633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have Khumeia propose that the consilium make the new magi their own cabal as a sort of training group. If you've read Broken Diamond, basically the Cruicible from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sending 'open letter' to all involved cabals and arranging Consilium meeting on the matter, with PCs working as 'heralds', sounds as good task idea. It also is with a jive of <i>Khuemia</i>'s position as local Councilor and Deacon, with Hierarch seat aspirations. Multi-person Awakening of PCs also goes in favor of that idea.<br /> <br /> Question is on the <i>Dead Wrens</i> - They are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=958244#post958244\">recast by me as Libertines (almost) sole cabal</a> and by <b>Boston Unveiled </b>they are apolitical. <b>Would this traditional Libertines agreed to plan of Counsilium?</b> Not to mention all the bad blood with <i>Shadow Chorus</i> over Emerald Scroll thing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=958633#post958633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a SL Deacon I'm guessing Khumeia probably can't want to get rid of them, but I could see her being quite annoyed none the less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you explain more this? I cannot understand this sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-27-2016, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T05:43:22-07:00","id":958701,"title":"","content":"Forming a cabal can be done any number of ways depending on the context of the Consilium. For instance its possible for members of the prospective cabal to go to the Consilium and say that they're a cabal and gain official recognition. Or they could just start to act like a cabal even without official recognition until it's just accepted that they are in fact a cabal (Kind of the common law way of doing it). Or the mentors could petition the Consilium to put the prospective members together to form a cabal. Or the mentors could just push them together and tell them to get along and let the Mages figure out on their own if the work as a cabal or not. I could keep going, there are a lot of options. <br /> <br /> Anyway, you don't -need- the PCs to be in the same cabal. All you really need is for them to work on the same plots and design those to encourage collaboration or at least familiarization with each other. If you can get them to work together often enough then you can start subtly exerting outside pressure to make them prefer working with each other rather than others. This could lead to them eventually forming a cabal organically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:01:38-07:00","id":958706,"title":"","content":"Have you worked out metal laws of your Consilium? Things like this should arrive organically from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:40:02-07:00","id":958752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=958635#post958635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question - Thing that was not clear to me in reading of <b>Sanctum &amp; Sigil</b> - <b>Do mentors need direct Consilium meeting on forming cabal?</b> Or do they only need to agree with themselves? Like, do I need to announce whole Ruling Council meeting - or just that <i>Brotherhood</i>, <i>Chorus</i> and <i>Wrens</i> meet and agree to forming the cabal from their new apprentices?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can do that themselves, but the reason I bring the consilium in is I thnk it serves Khumeia's purposes better to make it an official consilia policy. It adds to the pressure on the group, whilst also potentially making it easier to claim the glory if it somehow succeeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would this traditional Libertines agreed to plan of Counsilium?[/B] Not to mention all the bad blood with <i>Shadow Chorus</i> over Emerald Scroll thing... </div> </div> </div>I doubt the Wrens would care too much. The SC could plausibly see the new cabal as a good way to monitor the Wrens and these two new FC members.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you explain more this? I cannot understand this sentence. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sorry. I knew that wasn't a great sentence. The Silver Ladder ideology heavily pushes the idea that magi should be working together, and Khumeia seems pretty idealistic, therefore I think even if the cabal have really annoyed her, she'd probably at least try to still work with them. If you follow this plan, she's sorta helping them, but also hurting them at the same time.<br /> <br /> In comparison, if the cabal had done that with the Nemean, he'd probably at the very least beat them up and take their book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T09:02:40-07:00","id":958761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=958752#post958752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt the Wrens would care too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what can <i>Khumeia</i> do so the <i>Wrens</i> agree to full 'cabal making' under Ruling Council supervision? I do not know about any leverage she could have on them to coerce them in the whole thing. To me <i>Wrens</i> relation with Consilium sounds a lot like 'we are <i>totally </i>from different world, don't bother us'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=958752#post958752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In comparison, if the cabal had done that with the Nemean, he'd probably at the very least beat them up and take their book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I imagine this that way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T09:20:45-07:00","id":958764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=958761#post958761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what can <i>Khumeia</i> do so the <i>Wrens</i> agree to full 'cabal making' under Ruling Council supervision? I do not know about any leverage she could have on them to coerce them in the whole thing. To me <i>Wrens</i> relation with Consilium sounds a lot like 'we are <i>totally </i>from different world, don't bother us'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant, I don't think the Wrens would care to object.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, the Wrens run the Emerald Scroll which is pretty much the focus for the Boston mage community, they do have an interest in keeping the consilium on side.<br /> <br /> I remember Malcolm once mentioned in passing that the existence of the Emerald Scroll was the result of the Nemean's lax policing. I'd guess that a bar where magi hang out is generally seen as a borderline Violation of the veil at best. They're quite vulnerable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:19:07-07:00","id":958786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=958764#post958764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind, the Wrens run the Emerald Scroll which is pretty much the focus for the Boston mage community, they do have an interest in keeping the consilium on side.<br /> <br /> I remember Malcolm once mentioned in passing that the existence of the Emerald Scroll was the result of the Nemean's lax policing. I'd guess that a bar where magi hang out is generally seen as a borderline Violation of the veil at best. They're quite vulnerable.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, more or less, this situation:<br /> <i>Khumeia</i> - 'Agree to Consilium rulings or we will need to reevaluate your lax taking on Precept of Secrecy in Boston,,,'<br /> <br /> Yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:20:11-07:00","id":958814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929782-tasks-for-novice-mages?p=958786#post958786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, more or less, this situation:<br /> <i>Khumeia</i> - 'Agree to Consilium rulings or we will need to reevaluate your lax taking on Precept of Secrecy in Boston,,,'<br /> <br /> Yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, yeah. Though I doubt she'd ever say it that bluntly, maybe more 'If you cooperate with the consilium and show you're a team player then we'll know we can trust you not to violate the secrecy precept'. That is to say, a fair and equitable deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}